    "notes": "Closed score -> FOUR parts (Soprano, Alto, Tenor, Bass), D major 3/4, 12 bars, two verses under the Soprano.  Extreme ledger-line notes: Soprano D6 and C#6 (bar 8), A5/B5 often; Alto A3 (2 ledger lines below the treble staff, bar 1); Tenor up to A4 (above 3 ledger lines over the bass staff, bars 7 and 10); Bass down to A1 (3 ledger lines below the bass staff, bars 3, 5, 11) and B1 (bars 2, 7).  The alto/tenor ledger lines intrude into the lyric band between the staves.  Pencil sharps/flats drawn next to some notes in the scans only REMIND of the existing key-signature/accidental pitch (they agree with the truth); pencil circles, breath marks and words are not music."
